# B12: the community home on a phone. Signing in lands on the first community, whose route settles
# on its text channel, and a phone shows the community's home (its channels and rooms, the left
# pane), as the web's phone home does, not the chat. The chat isn't on screen there, so nothing is
# marked read: a message posted while the home shows leaves the channel unread. A channel row opens
# the chat, Back is the home again, Settings' Close returns to the home it was opened from, and a
# `semaphore://community/...` link shows the home too.
app 390 844
wait idle
click auth-connect
wait core session signed-out within 5
wait idle
click auth-username
type "alexk"
click auth-password
type "hunter2"
click auth-login
wait core session signed-in
# The route settles on #general, though its chat isn't shown.
wait core route channel/$ID(cc-general)
wait core connection connected
# In front, as a user's window is: a chat on screen would be marked read.
window activate

# 1. The landing: the home, with no composer drawn, and nothing marked read.
wait core element channel-$ID(cc-general)
wait core no-element composer/field
wait idle
shot 01-home
wait core requests markAsRead == 0 within 2

# 2. A message while the home shows: #general turns unread, and still nothing is marked read.
server post_as "{\"channelId\": \"$ID(cc-general)\", \"authorId\": \"$ID(u-priya)\", \"text\": \"posted while the home shows\"}"
wait core w9 unread $ID(cc-general) 1 within 5
wait core requests markAsRead == 0 within 2
wait idle
shot 02-home-unread

# 3. A channel row: the chat, which is read now.
click channel-$ID(cc-general)
wait core channel $ID(cc-general)
wait core element composer/field
wait core no-element channel-$ID(cc-general)
wait core requests markAsRead >= 1 within 5
wait core w9 unread $ID(cc-general) 0 within 5
wait idle
shot 03-chat

# 4. Back: the home again.
click phone-back
wait core element channel-$ID(cc-general)
wait core no-element composer/field

# 5. Settings from the home, then Close: the home it was opened from, not the chat.
click dock-all
wait core element sheet-settings
click sheet-settings
wait core route settings
click settings-close
wait core route channel
wait core element channel-$ID(cc-general)
wait core no-element composer/field

# 6. From the chat, a link to the community: the home, though the route settles on the channel.
click channel-$ID(cc-general)
wait core element composer/field
link "semaphore://community/$ID(c-couch)"
wait core route channel/$ID(cc-general)
wait core element channel-$ID(cc-general)
wait core no-element composer/field
wait idle
shot 04-home-from-link
